    {
      "title": "Rubio meets Adani, Tata Sons chiefs ahead of Reliance Jamnagar visit",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/rubio-meets-adani-tata-sons-chiefs-ahead-of-reliance-jamnagar-visit-126102100606_1.html",
      "description": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio met Adani Group chairman Gautam Adani and Tata Sons chairman N Chandrasekaran in Mumbai on Wednesday morning before heading to Jamnagar in Gujarat to visit Reliance Industries' giant oil-refining complex, the world's largest single-site refinery, along with Vantara and giga factories being developed by the conglomerate.\nRubio, who arrived in Mumbai on Tuesday afternoon, first met Adani, followed by a meeting with Chandrasekaran, sources said.\nNeither side released details of the meetings.\nAdani heads one of India's largest conglomerates, with interests spanning ports, airports, energy, logistics and infrastructure. The group has also been expanding its renewable-energy and manufacturing businesses, sectors that are central to India's ambitions to strengthen domestic supply chains and attract global investment.\nChandrasekaran, who leads Tata Sons, the Tata Group's holding company, oversees a sprawling business empire with interests in automobiles, .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-21T09:14:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "US State Secy Marco Rubio arrives in Jamnagar to visit Reliance refinery",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/us-state-secy-marco-rubio-arrives-in-jamnagar-to-visit-reliance-refinery-126102100485_1.html",
      "description": "US Secretary of State Marco Rubio arrived in Gujarat's Jamnagar city on Wednesday to visit the oil refinery complex owned by Mukesh Ambani-led Reliance Industries Ltd, a day after he described India as a crude oil refining \"superpower\".\nRubio is on a three-day visit to India to advance bilateral ties in energy, trade and investment, defence and critical technologies, besides exchanging views on the West Asia crisis.\nDuring his visit, Rubio is scheduled to tour the Jamnagar refinery complex, which assumes significance in the context of his remarks on India's oil refining capabilities and his call for processing more Venezuelan crude in the country.\nAccording to the RIL website, its Jamnagar refinery is the \"largest and most complex single-site refinery in the world with 1.4 million barrels per day (MMBPD) crude processing capacity and a complexity index of 21.1 - the highest in the world\".\nIt states that \"the refinery has processed over 216 different grades of crude oil produced in",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-21T08:08:50"
    },
